WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
A demonstration with drawn screens: one product, built by a team of coding agents.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.500
You bring the idea. In a terminal, install.sh --wizard opens the setup page.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.500
The first screen says what it found in your folder and proposes a way to work.

4
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.500
Install the kit: its files go beside your code. Nothing is committed or pushed.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.500
Confirm the rules, then register a second identity that reviews every change.

6
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.500
Publish sends the kit to main. Your idea and plan wait for your approval.

7
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.500
Write your idea in one line. Your coding agent drafts the plan.

8
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.000
Each task lists the checks it must pass. You approve by typing the folder's name.

9
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.500
Start this agent opens a terminal with it; below it, the same command to copy.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.500
The last screen follows the project, and your app's link once it is deployed.

11
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.000
Each agent claims its own task and its files, and writes the failing test first.

12
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.500
Another identity reviews each change; approved work merges into main, one at a time.

13
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.000
Every task of the plan is a square. It turns green when its work is merged.

14
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The dashboard: point at a square to see what it waits for and what it unblocks.

15
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
What waits for you comes first. An approved change merges once the checks pass.

16
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Agents: one card each, with its task and when it was last seen.

17
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.000
Edit arranges the summary: move, hide or add blocks.

18
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Share turns the progress into an image to post.
